course: dictionary
lesson: 3678
title: A word from the map
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about places, and the clues around them can help you understand. «The fjords of Norway are U-shaped valleys later flooded by the sea.» A valley is low land between hills, and the sea is salt water, so a fjord is a place where the sea has come into the land.
explain: «A fjord is a deep U-shaped valley carved by a glacier and later flooded by the sea.» A glacier is a huge, slow river of ice. Carved means cut out over a long time. The clue is «later»: the ice did the cutting first, and the sea came in afterwards.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «They sailed along a fjord between high cliffs.» Put in "a long, narrow, deep inlet of the sea between high cliffs" and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Fjord is also spelt fiord, especially in New Zealand. The spelling is different, but the word means the same thing. When you meet a new spelling, look at the sentence for clues before you give up.
fact: A fjord is a long, narrow, deep inlet of the sea between high cliffs.
fact: A fjord was made by a glacier long ago, and the sea later flowed into the valley it carved.
fact: «Norwegian fjords» are famous, and fjords are also found in New Zealand, Canada, Chile and Greenland.
fact: Milford Sound in New Zealand is a famous fjord that people sail along.
fact: Fjord can also be spelt «fiord», especially in New Zealand.
exercise: What is a fjord? | A hot, dry plain with no water | A tall mountain with snow on top | *A long, narrow, deep inlet of the sea between high cliffs
exercise: «A fjord is a deep U-shaped valley carved by a glacier.» What made the fjord? | A hurricane of wind | *A glacier, a slow river of ice, long ago | A volcano erupting | A farmer digging a ditch
exercise: Which country is famous for «Norwegian fjords»? | *Norway | Spain | Egypt | Mongolia
test: Fjord can also be spelt how, especially in New Zealand? | *Fiord | Fyord | Forde | Fjurd
test: «The sea flooded the valley.» In a fjord, what happened to the valley? | It was dried up by the sun | It was turned into a lake of mud | *It was flooded by the sea | It was filled with sand
exam: Which sentence uses fjord correctly? | The fjord was a hot desert with cactus plants | We ate a fjord for lunch | *They took a boat trip along the fjord between the steep cliffs | Her fjord was the tallest in the class
